.SH "NAME"
tlenv \- manage your TeX Live environment
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fBtlenv\fP \fI<command>\fP [\fI<args>\fP...]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
tlenv respects the \fI.texlive\-version\fP file in a project directory by making sure that any \fBtlmgr\fP, \fBtex\fP, \fBlatex\fP, or other TeX Live command invocation automatically invokes the TeX Live version configured for that project.
.sp
It does so by generating shims for all TeX Live executables. As long as tlenv shims directory is prepended to PATH, tlenv automatically ensures transparent switching between TeX Live versions.
.sp
tlenv looks for available TeX Live versions in the \fI$TLENV_ROOT/versions\fP directory. Since TeX Live keeps its executables in a platform\-specific subdirectory, the actual programs are found under \fI$TLENV_ROOT/versions/<version>/bin/<platform>\fP.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.sp
\fBtlenv global\fP [\fI<version>\fP]
.RS 4
View or change the global TeX Live version
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv local\fP [\fI<version>\fP]
.RS 4
View or change the local TeX Live version
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv shell\fP [\fI<version>\fP]
.RS 4
View or change the TeX Live version for the current shell session
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv version\fP
.RS 4
View the currently active TeX Live version and where it is set from
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv versions\fP
.RS 4
List all locally installed TeX Live versions known to tlenv
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv install\fP [\fI<version>\fP]
.RS 4
(Provided by the \fBtexlive\-install\fP plugin) Download and install a new TeX Live version
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv rehash\fP
.RS 4
Regenerate shims for all known TeX Live executables
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv which\fP [\fI<command>\fP]
.RS 4
View the executable path that a command resolves to
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv init\fP
.RS 4
Help bootstrap tlenv into the current shell environment
.RE
.sp
\fBtlenv help\fP [\fI<command>\fP]
.RS 4
View help text for any tlenv command
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
.sp
\fBTLENV_VERSION\fP (default: read from \fI.texlive\-version\fP file)
.RS 4
The TeX Live version name to be used
.RE
.sp
\fBTLENV_ROOT\fP (default: \fI~/.tlenv\fP)
.RS 4
The location where tlenv discovers TeX Live versions, plugins, and other configuration
.RE
.sp
\fBTLENV_DEBUG\fP
.RS 4
Activates printing debug information about tlenv internals to standard error
.RE
.sp
\fBTLENV_HOOK_PATH\fP
.RS 4
Colon\-separated list of paths searched for tlenv plugin scripts
.RE
.sp
\fBTLENV_DIR\fP (default: \fI$PWD\fP)
.RS 4
Directory to traverse bottom\-up to locate the \fI.texlive\-version\fP file
.RE
.SH "PLUGINS"
.sp
As its core functionality, tlenv only switches between TeX Live versions and does nothing else, but offers a plugin mechanism to hook into and override almost any aspect of its default behavior.
.sp
The most common plugin for tlenv is \fBtexlive\-install\fP which facilitates installing new TeX Live versions into the \fI$TLENV_ROOT/versions\fP directory.
